-- title:
--   Factorisation of a function on an annulus into translates of the parameter
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, and $F$ a field that is an $L$-algebra. Let `An` be an annulus of $F$ over $A$: a set $\mathrm{dom}$ of places of $F/L$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing $L$, proper, with principal ideals), a parameter $z =$ `An.param` $\in F$ and a modulus in the maximal ideal of $A$, such that each $P \in \mathrm{dom}$ has residue field generated by $L$, has $z$ in its valuation ring with value $z(P) := P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,z$ a nonzero element of the maximal ideal of $A$ dividing the modulus by a further element of that ideal, such that each admissible value is attained by exactly one place of $\mathrm{dom}$, such that $\mathrm{ord}_P(z - z(P)) = 1$, together with the unit principle for functions without zeros or poles on $\mathrm{dom}$. Assume that every nonzero $f \in F$ has $\mathrm{ord}_P f \ne 0$ for only finitely many $P \in \mathrm{dom}$, where $\mathrm{ord}_P$ is the normalised integer valuation attached to $P$. Then for every nonzero $f \in F$ there are a finite set $s$ of places contained in $\mathrm{dom}$, a function $n : \mathrm{Place}\,L\,F \to \mathbb{Z}$ and a nonzero $g \in F$ with $\mathrm{ord}_P g = 0$ for all $P \in \mathrm{dom}$, such that $f = g \cdot \prod_{P \in s} (z - z(P))^{n(P)}$.
--
--   This is the Weierstrass-type factorisation of a function on an annulus: its divisor on the annulus is supported on the places of the domain, and there the uniformisers may be taken to be the translates $z - z(P)$ of the parameter. It is the first step in the analysis of functions on the interior-circle charts, used in the construction of the Gauss ring homomorphism to the rational function field, in the description of the induced valuation subrings, and in the slope laws for such charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Annulus_exists_eq_mul_prod_param_sub_zpow.lean

